From 1314277be5633c92d8d0abb6ed8a76bd2362b9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malachi Willey <malwilley@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Apr 2025 10:00:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ref(tests): Change default testing behavior to use in-memory
 router instead of mocks (#90490)

Ref https://github.com/getsentry/frontend-tsc/issues/85

HUGE change, but only to test files. This change ensures that all tests
with `render()` will use the in-memory router unless a flag is provided,
which is much preferred to the old method of mocking everything. Tests
relying on the old behavior now include `deprecatedRouterMocks` so they
continue passing.

Changes:

- Rename `enableRouterMocks` to `deprecatedRouterMocks`
- Change `render()` default to no longer use the deprecated router mocks
- Modifies failing tests (which relied on the old router mocks) to
include `deprecatedRouterMocks: true`
- Cleans up any unnecessary inclusions of `router` mocks being passed to
`render` (necessary to include here because the render() typing causes
an error when this happens)
